    "content" : "My <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"ot-hashtag\" href=\"https://plus.google.com/s/%23Digispark\">#Digispark</a> from Kickstarter came in today. I backed one board and the RGB LED shield. I ran into some problems after installing the driver, which required a reboot of my computer, but has ran fine since. It uses the Arduino IDE, but has a hacky way of programming it. You have to hit upload on the program, then it will tell you when to plug the board into one of your USB ports. It is made so it is in programming mode for 5 seconds upon initial power-up and then it switches over and runs the stored code. I&#39;m not sure what I&#39;m going to do with it yet, but it does fit pretty nice on the side of my computer. Maybe I&#39;ll just run the demo that cycles through the LED&#39;s colors all the time.",
    "objectType" : "note",
    "originalContent" : "My #Digispark from Kickstarter came in today. I backed one board and the RGB LED shield. I ran into some problems after installing the driver, which required a reboot of my computer, but has ran fine since. It uses the Arduino IDE, but has a hacky way of programming it. You have to hit upload on the program, then it will tell you when to plug the board into one of your USB ports. It is made so it is in programming mode for 5 seconds upon initial power-up and then it switches over and runs the stored code. I'm not sure what I'm going to do with it yet, but it does fit pretty nice on the side of my computer. Maybe I'll just run the demo that cycles through the LED's colors all the time.",
